The final act of\'a0
\f1\i Tears of the Kingdom
\f0\i0 \'a0kicks in once you get all five Sage\'92s Vows and uncover the twelve Dragon Tears across Hyrule, finally revealing the location of the Master Sword. A final flashback reveals that Zelda turned herself into a Divine Dragon by swallowing her Secret Stone. By embedding the Master Sword in her new body, Zelda spends millennia pouring her light essence into the weapon, restoring and empowering it beyond anything before.\
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa431\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 To get the Master Sword back, Link has to land on the dragon and literally tear it from its head. Sadly, however, Zelda remains in dragon form and simply flies away. With the sword of light in hand Link is finally ready to confront Ganondorf. Through some recon in the Depths, you learn the Demon King has made his base far beneath Hyrule Castle, deeper than you\'92ve ever ventured before.\
With the help of the Sages, Link traverses the network of tunnels at the bottom of the Depths, and confronts Ganondorf one-on-one. The Demon King\'92s designs are simple \'97 he only wants to reform Hyrule in his image and rule over everything as the ultimate king.\
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa431\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 After two nail-biting fights, Ganondorf follows in Zelda\'92s footsteps and swallows the Secret Stone that\'92s been giving him power, turning into a massive demonic dragon. Link is fired high into Hyrule\'92s sky with Ganondorf. Just in the nick of time, Zelda appears to help the hero in a massive dragon-versus-dragon battle. After destroying all the Eyes of Malice on Ganondorf\'92s body, Link uses the Master Sword to break the villain\'92s Secret Stone, resulting in a massive explosion.\
While the Demon King explodes, it\'92s not entirely clear if this is a definitive end or if Ganondorf\'92s long cycle of rebirth will continue into future entries.\
After the battle, Link is transported into some kind of ethereal realm, where the spirits of Rauru and Sonia appear. Using Link\'92s arm and their own power, the trio restore Princess Zelda\'92s original body. As Ruaru and Sonia disappear, so does the arena Link and Zelda are standing in.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Link and Zelda reappear in Hyrule\'92s sky and plummet toward the ground. Link has to dive toward Zelda and catch her, then they both safely land in a pool of water.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa431\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Zelda awakens and tells Link she felt a \'93warm, loving embrace,\'94 and she concludes that her sacrifice helped to finally beat the Demon King. As the Gloom corruption starts to fall off of Hyrule Castle in the distance, Zelda tells Link she saw Hyrule at its peak when she was dreaming and has \'93so much\'94 to tell him.\
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa431\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 After the credits roll we\'92re treated to one final scene, with Zelda, Link, and all the sages standing at the altar where the princess first turned into a dragon. Mineru says she wanted to share the view with her friends one final time, and tells the group that Hyrule\'92s safety is now up to them, just before she fades out of existence.\
Zelda now addresses the group and talks about how Rauru and Sonia dreamt of an eternal peace for Hyrule, and how she wants to carry on that dream. Each of the Sages confirm their dedication, and that of their descendants, to seeing that dream through.\
Overall it feels like a fairly definitive ending, but so did\'a0
\f1\i Breath of the Wild
\f0\i0 \'a0at the time. We\'92ve still only seen a few flashbacks of ancient Hyrule, and considering how Zelda says she saw \'93so much,\'94 it\'92s certainly possible we could see more development on that end. For now, we\'92ll have to wait and see what Nintendo has in store next.\
